# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Adam Hložný et al. (2026). Upscaling DFT-trained machine-learning interatomic potential toward Quantum Monte Carlo accuracy: Sulfur-vacancy migration in monolayer MoS$_2$ as a testbed.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2605.22601  arXiv:2605.22601v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2605.22601v1 (sha256 e622b111e09b9c31...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 489 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/hlozny2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the DFT-PBE MACE of the authors' earlier work (the
# baseline DFT-MLIP), its readout-only fine-tuning to FN-DMC energies
# with a thresholded penalty on deviations from DFT forces (FT-MLIP), and
# the analogous fine-tuning to HSE06 energies as a proxy; the stated
# force MAE against FN-DMC finite-difference derivatives and the
# validation energy RMSE. Migration barriers and free-energy barriers
# are properties.

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
